EXPERIMENTAL, DEFAULT-OFF: "Zen 5c-first soft park" scheduler series
(local carry for ROG Zephyrus G16 GA605KM battery testing; NOT for upstream)

Five changes, combined and rebased onto linux-omarchy 7.2.8-9 (applies after
all other patches at fuzz 0):
  1. platform/x86/amd/hfi: optional ITMT ranking (performance / efficiency /
     inverted) via sysfs `ranking` and `amd_hfi.ranking=` (default performance).
  2. sched/fair: soft wakeup CPU preference behind a static key (off).
  3. x86/amd: optional workload-class tracking/steering behind static keys (off).
  4. sched/fair: optional SMT packing inside the preferred set (off).
  5. sched/fair: prefer an idle preferred CPU as the NOHZ idle-load balancer
     (only when a preference is set).

Nothing is enabled by this package: no cmdline, udev rule or sysctl. With the
knobs at their defaults the scheduler takes the stock paths. Status:
compile-tested only, pending battery A/B measurements on the target laptop.

